Z||000000||Will||07-27-2000||04:22 PM||||Greetings!<P>I have posted to this forum before about using an LS1 ECM to run a '95 Northstar.<BR>The idea occured to me the other day, though, of using an LT5 ECM (from a ZR1 Corvette).<BR>I have a couple of questions that I was hoping someone here could answer:<BR>Does anyone know how similar the crankshaft and camshaft position sensors are between the two engines? I heard that a portion of the design of the LT5 was carried over to the Northstar.<P>I also have afew general questions about the LT5:<BR>Does the LT5 use a camshaft position sensor?<BR>Does the LT5 use a mass air flow (MAF) sensor?<BR>The LT5 is a waste spark coil pack engine, isn't it?<BR>Does it use batch fire injection or sequential?<BR>How many knock sensors does it use?<P>Has anyone ever worked with an LT5 or have any information at all that might be remotely applicable?<P>Thank you for your time.||||reg||1
